WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:01:17.330
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
01:17.600 --> 01:18.670
I have to make it happen.

3
01:40.300 --> 01:43.200
Hello? Okay, okay. I'll be right there.

4
01:43.770 --> 01:44.570
Mm-hmm.

5
02:02.330 --> 02:03.130
I'm here.

6
02:04.730 --> 02:05.530
Took you long enough.

7
02:06.470 --> 02:07.270
Sigh!

8
02:08.600 --> 02:11.100
In an industry where everything changes faster than trends...

9
02:11.270 --> 02:12.070
Oh!

10
02:12.730 --> 02:13.530
What is it?

11
02:15.270 --> 02:16.070
Look at this.

12
02:18.100 --> 02:19.600
Nannalin Thawarak.

13
02:19.600 --> 02:24.170
Her name has become the talk of the fashion and publishing industries

14
02:24.170 --> 02:27.870
since she transformed the image of a long-established magazine

15
02:27.870 --> 02:30.630
and made it influential again in the digital age.

16
02:30.630 --> 02:32.000
Over the past two years...

17
02:32.570 --> 02:35.500
she has received rising executive awards from several institutions

18
02:35.500 --> 02:38.570
for her leadership and for bringing print media

19
02:38.570 --> 02:40.700
back into the spotlight among younger generations.

20
02:40.970 --> 02:42.000
There's your witch.

21
02:42.000 --> 02:43.100
She's in the news again.

22
02:43.570 --> 02:46.800
Don't call her a witch. She's gorgeous!

23
02:47.800 --> 02:48.370
Why?

24
02:48.370 --> 02:49.370
What should I call her, then?

25
02:49.370 --> 02:51.530
The angel of the fashion industry?

26
02:55.530 --> 02:56.670
She's so cool!

27
02:58.370 --> 02:59.570
What's so cool about her?

28
02:59.570 --> 03:01.500
Seriously, what's cool?

29
03:02.870 --> 03:06.100
People fear her because she's brilliant.

30
03:07.300 --> 03:09.730
That's quite a romantic way to justify being scary.

31
03:11.500 --> 03:15.300
Namkhing, look! She's not just beautiful.

32
03:15.300 --> 03:17.100
She's incredibly powerful.

33
03:17.100 --> 03:20.930
It's like... wherever she goes, people have to listen.

34
03:21.730 --> 03:23.370
You're losing it.

35
03:24.570 --> 03:27.730
Just watch. One day, I'll be like her.

36
03:28.130 --> 03:28.870
Like what?

37
03:28.870 --> 03:29.730
Beautiful?

38
03:31.170 --> 03:32.100
You're already beautiful, honey.

39
03:32.600 --> 03:35.630
I mean I'll be as capable as her, and...

40
03:35.630 --> 03:37.800
people will recognize me for my work.

41
03:38.570 --> 03:40.270
Here comes the inspirational speech.

42
03:40.530 --> 03:42.500
Oh, I've got goosebumps!

43
03:43.470 --> 03:44.270
Are you teasing me?

44
03:45.730 --> 03:47.430
No, I'm not.

45
03:47.430 --> 03:50.800
I'm so moved, I could cry.

46
03:50.800 --> 03:51.470
Hey!

47
03:54.570 --> 03:55.770
But seriously,

48
03:55.770 --> 03:59.130
she's beautiful and talented. No argument there.

49
03:59.130 --> 04:02.330
Still, those rumors are pretty scary.

50
04:02.330 --> 04:03.400
You know, that she's...

51
04:03.400 --> 04:04.200
ruthless.

52
04:04.200 --> 04:05.770
A perfectionist about everything.

53
04:05.770 --> 04:07.600
If anyone messes up in front of her,

54
04:08.400 --> 04:09.430
well...

55
04:09.430 --> 04:11.300
they practically won't survive at the office.

56
04:11.770 --> 04:14.200
Come on! Isn't that an exaggeration?

57
04:15.470 --> 04:16.430
I heard

58
04:16.430 --> 04:17.829
she's demanding, too.

59
04:17.829 --> 04:19.500
She always gets what she wants.

60
04:19.500 --> 04:22.470
The work has to match exactly what she envisions.

61
04:25.070 --> 04:28.470
But what if what she wants actually improves the company?

62
04:29.400 --> 04:30.970
Someone that capable

63
04:30.970 --> 04:34.330
can't be a sweet angel all the time, can she?

64
04:35.000 --> 04:38.100
If she weren't so precise and detail-oriented,

65
04:38.100 --> 04:41.000
how could she lead such a huge company forward?

66
04:42.170 --> 04:42.970
Oh, please!

67
04:43.400 --> 04:44.870
You've been hypnotized.

68
04:46.470 --> 04:48.270
I admire her, okay?

69
04:49.400 --> 04:50.200
Okay.

70
04:50.570 --> 04:52.500
I'll stop teasing you, Miss Alice-

71
04:53.100 --> 04:56.300
future powerhouse female executive.

72
04:58.970 --> 04:59.800
Just you wait.

73
05:00.700 --> 05:01.500
Then wait and see.

74
05:05.100 --> 05:05.900
No need to watch anymore.

75
05:11.970 --> 05:12.830
Oh?

76
05:12.830 --> 05:15.330
Let's change the channel from female executives

77
05:15.330 --> 05:17.300
to your real-life girlfriend.

78
05:19.300 --> 05:20.300
Hello, Namhom?

79
05:21.130 --> 05:21.870
Alice.

80
05:21.870 --> 05:23.500
Can you come see me?

81
05:23.500 --> 05:24.200
Right now.

82
05:25.000 --> 05:25.900
Is something wrong?

83
05:26.370 --> 05:28.400
I just want you to be the first person I tell.

84
05:28.400 --> 05:29.770
That's all.

85
05:31.670 --> 05:32.470
Hey!

86
05:32.970 --> 05:33.800
Where are you going?

87
05:34.070 --> 05:35.300
Class is about to start!

88
05:35.770 --> 05:36.870
Take my handouts for me!

89
05:37.500 --> 05:38.400
Hey! Hey!

90
05:39.170 --> 05:39.970
Hey!

91
05:40.100 --> 05:41.870
Am I your friend or your filing cabinet?

92
05:42.070 --> 05:43.670
You're my very best friend!

93
05:44.100 --> 05:44.900
Take this, too. Here!

94
05:53.130 --> 05:55.330
You sure run fast when it's for love.

95
06:04.070 --> 06:05.400
Namhom, what's wrong?

96
06:05.400 --> 06:06.370
Why are you crying?

97
06:27.100 --> 06:28.470
I passed the audition!

98
06:29.770 --> 06:30.570
Really?

99
06:30.600 --> 06:31.400
Mm-hmm.

100
06:31.770 --> 06:34.470
See? I told you you'd make it, Namhom.

101
06:35.770 --> 06:36.570
At first,

102
06:37.570 --> 06:39.800
I was sure I wouldn't pass.

103
06:39.800 --> 06:41.770
My hands were shaking,

104
06:41.770 --> 06:43.600
and my voice almost cracked.

105
06:44.500 --> 06:46.470
But you passed! See?

106
06:46.470 --> 06:49.100
I told you you're amazing, Namhom.

107
06:52.100 --> 06:53.870
You're the first person I've told, Alice.

108
06:56.000 --> 06:56.970
From now on,

109
06:56.970 --> 06:58.770
you'll have to practice even harder.

110
06:58.770 --> 07:00.630
And eat your meals on time.

111
07:00.630 --> 07:01.770
No staying up late.

112
07:02.800 --> 07:03.930
Got it?

113
07:04.400 --> 07:06.500
You sound like a celebrity manager.

114
07:06.800 --> 07:08.470
I could be one for you.

115
07:08.470 --> 07:10.730
When you become super famous,

116
07:10.730 --> 07:13.200
I'll tell everyone...

117
07:13.200 --> 07:15.700
that I spotted your talent ages ago.

118
07:17.970 --> 07:19.770
Do you think I can do it, Alice?

119
07:21.870 --> 07:22.930
Of course you can.

120
07:22.930 --> 07:26.130
You're going to be a huge star, Namhom.

121
07:44.330 --> 07:45.700
What's wrong, Alice?

122
07:59.100 --> 08:00.330
They don't allow you to date?

123
08:02.170 --> 08:04.800
It's probably about the agency's image.

124
08:09.970 --> 08:10.770
But why?

125
08:12.570 --> 08:14.270
We're not doing anything wrong.

126
08:16.270 --> 08:17.730
I just love you, Alice.

127
08:21.130 --> 08:22.270
What's wrong with that?

128
08:26.500 --> 08:27.600
Then I won't sign it.

129
08:28.000 --> 08:28.770
That contract.

130
08:28.770 --> 08:29.470
Namhom.

131
08:34.070 --> 08:35.970
You earned this opportunity

132
08:37.070 --> 08:38.000
because you're talented.

133
08:41.669 --> 08:43.370
Please don't give it up for me.

134
08:45.600 --> 08:47.400
I don't want to lose you, Alice.

135
08:53.400 --> 08:54.900
I'm still right here.

136
08:56.900 --> 08:58.100
It's just that maybe...

137
08:58.100 --> 09:01.730
we'll have to be somewhere no one else can see us.

138
09:14.470 --> 09:16.170
That's so unfair.

139
09:20.770 --> 09:21.900
Yeah.

140
09:23.600 --> 09:24.930
It really is unfair.

141
09:42.700 --> 09:44.000
I love you, Alice.

142
09:46.200 --> 09:47.470
I love you too, Namhom.

143
09:49.530 --> 09:51.700
That's why I want you to follow your dream.

144
10:42.800 --> 10:44.600
Well, hello, girlfriend of the year!

145
10:44.600 --> 10:46.930
Good news so big you had to call me?

146
10:53.370 --> 10:55.730
Yeah. It's really great.

147
10:57.470 --> 10:58.430
Alice,

148
10:58.430 --> 11:00.070
what happened?

149
11:03.870 --> 11:04.930
Are you free tonight?

150
11:05.600 --> 11:07.000
Come hang out with me.

151
11:09.200 --> 11:10.000
What's going on?

152
11:18.970 --> 11:20.300
Nothing.

153
11:20.300 --> 11:22.170
I just feel like drinking.

154
11:25.370 --> 11:27.770
Celebrating with a voice like you're about to cry?

155
11:29.070 --> 11:30.900
Alice, what's going on with Namhom?

156
11:36.130 --> 11:37.770
Namhom passed her audition.

157
11:39.130 --> 11:41.400
Isn't that amazing news?

158
11:43.930 --> 11:45.000
It's wonderful.

159
11:45.000 --> 11:47.000
So wonderful that I have to...

160
11:47.000 --> 11:49.270
be really, really happy for her, right?

161
11:51.270 --> 11:52.870
Where are you? I'll come to you.

162
11:55.970 --> 11:58.300
Aren't you busy with something?

163
11:58.830 --> 11:59.670
You don't need to come.

164
12:01.770 --> 12:03.070
I am busy,

165
12:03.070 --> 12:04.530
but if you're crying,

166
12:04.530 --> 12:05.530
I can drop everything.

167
12:08.000 --> 12:09.900
Who's crying? I'm not crying!

168
12:12.470 --> 12:13.370
You...

169
12:13.370 --> 12:15.130
You're a terrible liar, yet you keep lying.

170
12:19.570 --> 12:21.470
I'll wait at our usual place.

171
12:21.470 --> 12:22.970
When you're done,

172
12:22.970 --> 12:24.330
come meet me there.

173
12:26.770 --> 12:28.700
Are you sure you'll be okay alone?

174
12:29.300 --> 12:30.230
Mm-hmm.

175
12:30.230 --> 12:31.830
I'm tough, remember?

176
12:34.070 --> 12:37.100
Okay, wait there. I'll join you soon.

177
12:37.100 --> 12:38.870
Don't drink too much before I get there.

178
12:40.200 --> 12:41.000
Okay.

179
12:41.600 --> 12:45.170
And... you don't have to be strong all the time.

180
12:45.170 --> 12:46.100
Understand?

181
12:48.000 --> 12:48.800
Mm-hmm.

182
13:58.000 --> 14:01.170
Sorry, something urgent came up.

183
14:01.370 --> 14:04.270
I'll be a little late.

184
14:46.470 --> 14:48.100
Isn't that Nannalin?

185
15:06.330 --> 15:07.400
Her zipper's open.

186
15:13.800 --> 15:14.930
Should I tell her?

187
15:30.130 --> 15:30.930
Sigh.

188
15:52.930 --> 15:53.730
Um...

189
15:56.000 --> 15:56.800
Excuse me.

190
16:00.400 --> 16:01.200
Excuse me.

191
16:12.800 --> 16:13.900
Here goes nothing.

192
18:02.970 --> 18:09.070
Two years later.

193
18:44.730 --> 18:45.400
Okay.

194
19:08.900 --> 19:09.700
I'm here.

195
19:10.800 --> 19:13.200
Future content creator extraordinaire!

196
19:13.630 --> 19:14.870
Is your voice shaking?

197
19:15.170 --> 19:15.970
No.

198
19:17.400 --> 19:18.970
Well, maybe a little.

199
19:19.730 --> 19:22.470
Girl, you prepared a portfolio like you're taking over the company.

200
19:22.470 --> 19:23.200
Don't be scared.

201
19:23.870 --> 19:26.200
But I just graduated,

202
19:26.200 --> 19:28.170
and I don't have any experience.

203
19:29.000 --> 19:29.700
You've got brains,

204
19:29.700 --> 19:30.800
passion,

205
19:30.800 --> 19:31.770
You've got a portfolio

206
19:31.770 --> 19:33.400
and superhuman determination.

207
19:33.700 --> 19:36.070
If they don't hire you, it's their loss.

208
19:36.600 --> 19:38.330
Yeah, thanks.

209
19:39.100 --> 19:40.200
And remember:

210
19:40.200 --> 19:42.900
Don't panic. Don't apologize every three sentences.

211
19:42.900 --> 19:43.870
And...

212
19:44.600 --> 19:45.400
What else?

213
19:45.870 --> 19:47.600
Be yourself as much as possible.

214
19:47.600 --> 19:49.600
Your angel will always bless you.

215
19:50.370 --> 19:50.870
Got it!

216
19:50.870 --> 19:53.370
This time, I'm not backing down.

217
19:54.400 --> 19:55.200
Mm-hmm.

218
19:55.570 --> 19:56.370
Talk later.

219
20:17.170 --> 20:18.270
Aranya, right?

220
20:18.930 --> 20:19.730
Yes.

221
20:20.170 --> 20:20.970
This way.

222
20:23.800 --> 20:26.600
Slow down, slow down. Don't panic. Don't panic.

223
20:32.530 --> 20:33.900
Please give us a brief introduction.

224
20:34.470 --> 20:36.000
Um, hello.

225
20:36.000 --> 20:38.530
I'm Aranya, but you can call me Alice.

226
20:38.530 --> 20:40.770
I graduated in marketing communications.

227
20:40.770 --> 20:43.370
I'm interested in fashion content

228
20:43.370 --> 20:46.000
and telling brand stories through people.

229
20:47.000 --> 20:47.570
Um...

230
20:47.570 --> 20:51.230
I believe fashion isn't just about clothing.

231
20:51.230 --> 20:52.770
It's a language

232
20:52.770 --> 20:54.900
people use to express who they are,

233
20:55.900 --> 20:57.470
how they want others to see them,

234
20:58.070 --> 21:00.530
and how they shape the way they're perceived.

235
21:01.130 --> 21:02.100
That's an interesting idea.

236
21:02.770 --> 21:04.930
Did you do all of this yourself?

237
21:05.500 --> 21:06.170
Yes.

238
21:06.170 --> 21:08.900
It's a hypothetical brief for a perfume brand.

239
21:08.900 --> 21:14.230
I started by asking how a woman should feel walking into a meeting room.

240
21:14.230 --> 21:16.170
Then I worked out the mood,

241
21:16.170 --> 21:17.070
the message,

242
21:17.070 --> 21:19.930
and found KOLs who could communicate that feeling.

243
21:20.570 --> 21:23.170
You have a good understanding of brand image.

244
21:24.130 --> 21:24.900
Thank you.

245
21:25.300 --> 21:26.870
I think...

246
21:26.870 --> 21:29.970
products don't just sell features.

247
21:29.970 --> 21:33.900
They sell the feeling people want when they use them.

248
21:34.670 --> 21:35.930
But it's a high-pressure environment here.

249
21:36.730 --> 21:37.570
Briefs change quickly,

250
21:37.970 --> 21:38.870
clients request endless revisions,

251
21:39.370 --> 21:40.600
and KOLs are hard to coordinate with.

252
21:41.070 --> 21:42.270
Even work you think is already good

253
21:42.670 --> 21:44.570
might be revised beyond recognition.

254
21:49.930 --> 21:50.770
Is it "Clean Food"?

255
21:51.070 --> 21:53.070
It has to be clean because of the body requirements.

256
21:55.000 --> 21:56.670
The legs... the legs are too big.

257
21:57.600 --> 21:59.100
Yes, the legs are too big.

258
22:10.970 --> 22:11.970
Here.

259
22:12.630 --> 22:14.070
I asked for the revised file,

260
22:14.070 --> 22:16.370
not excuses about why it isn't finished.

261
22:17.000 --> 22:18.430
I forgot to send it.

262
22:18.430 --> 22:21.370
My partner had to be rushed to the hospital,

263
22:21.370 --> 22:23.870
and they have no family, so I...

264
22:24.300 --> 22:25.530
During work hours?

265
22:26.400 --> 22:27.200
Yes.

266
22:27.930 --> 22:29.430
That document

267
22:29.830 --> 22:32.300
forced the client team to attend a meeting

268
22:32.300 --> 22:34.670
without any confirmed information.

269
22:34.670 --> 22:37.830
Without it, the KOL team followed the wrong schedule,

270
22:37.830 --> 22:40.970
and the client thought we were unprepared.

271
22:44.570 --> 22:45.800
I'm really sorry.

272
22:46.930 --> 22:48.270
Your partner...

273
22:48.270 --> 22:50.500
still needs treatment for quite a while, right?

274
22:51.730 --> 22:53.600
Yes, for several weeks.

275
22:56.070 --> 22:57.600
Then go home.

276
22:57.600 --> 22:59.430
Go take care of them.

277
22:59.430 --> 23:02.130
And don't come back. Not for a very long time.

278
23:03.330 --> 23:04.600
Do you think you can handle it?

279
23:07.170 --> 23:07.970
I can.

280
23:08.330 --> 23:09.730
I may not be the best yet,

281
23:10.130 --> 23:12.130
but I'm not afraid to start from zero.

282
23:12.400 --> 23:13.470
And I'm not afraid of hard work.

283
23:14.400 --> 23:15.300
Something's happened!

284
23:15.970 --> 23:17.770
The witch just fired Jang!

285
23:18.600 --> 23:19.870
And that's not all.

286
23:19.870 --> 23:20.900
She said...

287
23:20.900 --> 23:22.870
she needs a new assistant by today.

288
23:24.070 --> 23:25.630
Today, no exceptions!

289
23:25.630 --> 23:29.200
I'll go check on Jang. I don't know if she's okay.

290
23:29.470 --> 23:31.700
Where are we supposed to find someone today?

291
23:36.530 --> 23:37.330
Unless...

292
23:38.200 --> 23:39.000
What do you think?

293
23:39.000 --> 23:40.100
Her portfolio is pretty good.

294
23:41.800 --> 23:42.900
Alice?

295
23:43.470 --> 23:45.000
Do you still want to work here,

296
23:45.670 --> 23:47.500
even if it's not in content creation?

297
23:48.370 --> 23:49.330
What position is it?

298
23:57.470 --> 23:58.800
Ms. Nannalin?

299
24:00.000 --> 24:01.300
We've found someone.

300
24:03.370 --> 24:04.170
Mm.

301
24:04.600 --> 24:05.670
That was quick.

302
24:08.000 --> 24:10.270
I just hope she's not useless,

303
24:10.870 --> 24:12.700
irresponsible,

304
24:12.700 --> 24:14.600
so obsessed with her partner that she ruins her work,

305
24:14.770 --> 24:16.730
or completely incompetent.

306
24:17.730 --> 24:19.770
I don't have time to train...

307
24:19.770 --> 24:23.300
people who can't separate work from their personal lives.

308
24:25.930 --> 24:28.030
This candidate is quite good, Ms. Nannalin.

309
24:28.030 --> 24:29.700
Her work is strong,

310
24:29.700 --> 24:30.900
her portfolio is solid,

311
24:31.230 --> 24:33.470
she understands branding,

312
24:33.470 --> 24:35.270
and she can write articles.

313
24:39.300 --> 24:40.270
Write articles?

314
24:42.000 --> 24:42.800
Yes.

315
24:43.900 --> 24:46.300
She originally applied for the content creator position.

316
24:47.400 --> 24:49.500
Then why is she applying to be my assistant?

317
24:51.270 --> 24:52.200
Well...

318
24:52.200 --> 24:54.300
The thing is...

319
24:54.300 --> 24:57.130
our content creator position is already filled.

320
24:58.700 --> 25:00.800
The chairman's niece or nephew has taken the role.

321
25:02.370 --> 25:04.930
Of course.

322
25:07.170 --> 25:14.600
Give the content creator job to someone with connections, and send the person with real talent to be my assistant.

323
25:35.800 --> 25:36.770
Did she write this herself?

324
25:38.330 --> 25:40.770
Yes, I asked her questions,

325
25:41.700 --> 25:42.770
and she answered them. She definitely didn't memorize it.

326
25:43.200 --> 25:44.470
She definitely didn't memorize it.

327
25:49.870 --> 25:52.000
Are you all right, Ms. Nannalin?

328
25:56.000 --> 25:56.500
I'm fine.

329
25:57.930 --> 25:58.800
Send her in.

330
25:59.700 --> 26:00.500
Yes.

331
26:40.600 --> 26:42.070
Namkhing!

332
26:42.930 --> 26:44.270
Whoa!

333
26:44.970 --> 26:48.030
Well, look who finally decided to show up, Miss Busy Assistant!

334
26:48.030 --> 26:49.600
I thought they'd confiscated your phone.

335
26:50.000 --> 26:51.400
I'm lucky I even escaped.

336
26:54.470 --> 26:55.700
But your face...

337
26:58.000 --> 27:00.570
doesn't look like someone celebrating a new job.

338
27:01.330 --> 27:02.270
What's wrong with my face?

339
27:04.530 --> 27:08.330
You look like someone's sucked your soul out.

340
27:08.770 --> 27:12.400
I thought it was your dream agency! Blessed by the heavens, huh?

341
27:13.500 --> 27:16.770
More like a nightmare of magnitude ten!

342
27:18.000 --> 27:20.900
Oh! Is your boss really that scary?

343
27:22.730 --> 27:27.370
So scary I wanted to run away and become a nun on my first day!

344
27:30.670 --> 27:31.730
Okay, here's what we're doing.

345
27:32.430 --> 27:36.030
Tell me everything, starting from the second you stepped into the building.

346
27:36.030 --> 27:37.970
Don't leave out a single detail.

347
28:08.870 --> 28:11.170
Hello, I'm Aranya.

348
28:12.830 --> 28:15.070
You can call me Alice.

349
28:18.000 --> 28:21.370
What do you think my assistant's responsibilities are?

350
28:25.330 --> 28:30.230
Um, organizing tasks, coordinating work, supporting decisions,

351
28:30.600 --> 28:32.800
and making the boss's job easier.

352
28:37.170 --> 28:38.900
That sounds straight out of a job interview handbook.

353
28:46.470 --> 28:48.270
Then may I try answering again?

354
28:49.600 --> 28:50.400
Go ahead.

355
28:54.000 --> 28:56.730
An assistant shouldn't just follow orders.

356
28:56.730 --> 28:59.800
They should know which issues need the boss's attention

357
28:59.800 --> 29:01.770
and which can be handled

358
29:02.170 --> 29:03.530
before they ever reach the boss.

359
29:03.530 --> 29:07.570
Remember the details and coordinate everything thoroughly.

360
29:07.570 --> 29:09.800
And when there's something they don't know,

361
29:09.800 --> 29:13.300
ask clearly the first time instead of wasting time asking again.

362
29:17.900 --> 29:21.000
And what if your boss is extremely demanding?

363
29:21.730 --> 29:26.500
Then I'd need to learn what's being unreasonable

364
29:26.500 --> 29:28.570
and what's simply a work standard.

365
29:46.500 --> 29:47.400
Do you know who I am?

366
29:52.070 --> 29:55.500
Yes, I've seen you in the news.

367
29:56.870 --> 29:57.970
In the news?

368
29:58.700 --> 29:59.600
Yes.

369
30:03.970 --> 30:05.130
What about anywhere else?

370
30:32.670 --> 30:35.670
Um, I'm sorry...

371
30:37.270 --> 30:41.600
I don't mean to be disrespectful, but I just noticed...

372
30:42.130 --> 30:45.700
your zipper had slipped down, so...

373
30:45.970 --> 30:48.500
I only wanted to zip it up for you.

374
30:49.170 --> 30:49.900
Um...

375
30:51.270 --> 30:54.300
I wasn't trying to look, I mean...

376
30:58.100 --> 31:01.100
I did look, but not in that way!

377
31:06.200 --> 31:10.530
Do you often help strangers like this?

378
31:12.070 --> 31:14.300
No! This is the first time.

379
31:14.970 --> 31:19.800
I mean, my first time zipping up a stranger's clothes.

380
31:20.500 --> 31:21.930
Not my first time helping someone.

381
31:23.700 --> 31:28.200
I usually help people in more normal ways.

382
31:32.170 --> 31:32.830
Well, then...

383
31:34.230 --> 31:37.670
go ahead and finish zipping it up.

384
31:41.970 --> 31:42.770
Yes.

385
32:02.270 --> 32:03.400
Is something wrong with the outfit?

386
32:06.000 --> 32:08.070
Oh, no.

387
32:19.970 --> 32:21.870
Actually, maybe a little.

388
32:49.170 --> 32:50.100
All done.

389
32:53.530 --> 32:54.330
Thank you.

390
32:56.970 --> 32:57.700
You're welcome.

391
32:57.700 --> 32:58.500
Um...

392
32:58.570 --> 32:59.870
I'm sorry again.

393
33:03.800 --> 33:04.930
You apologize a lot.

394
33:08.300 --> 33:13.900
Well, I've gotten so many things wrong today.

395
33:15.300 --> 33:20.600
Next time you want to help someone, ask first.

396
33:25.670 --> 33:27.270
Yes, I'll remember that.

397
33:33.970 --> 33:34.770
Good.

398
38:56.070 --> 39:01.330
Um, a lot of people talk about you.

399
39:12.470 --> 39:15.670
If you're ready to start, read this in ten minutes.

400
39:15.970 --> 39:16.770
Huh?

401
39:17.130 --> 39:21.100
Then summarize what's holding this campaign back,

402
39:21.100 --> 39:25.670
who's responsible for what, and what needs fixing before noon.

403
39:28.170 --> 39:28.970
Of course.

404
39:30.370 --> 39:31.500
Any questions?

405
39:33.270 --> 39:36.500
Um, could I get access to the dashboard?

406
39:36.500 --> 39:40.070
I don't think this document alone will show the underlying issues.

407
39:41.100 --> 39:42.500
Ask the data team.

408
39:44.130 --> 39:44.930
Yes.

409
39:46.270 --> 39:47.900
Oh, and Alice.

410
39:48.600 --> 39:49.400
Yes?

411
39:50.470 --> 39:52.370
Next time you want to help me,

412
39:53.570 --> 39:55.200
ask me first.

413
39:57.300 --> 39:58.100
Of course.

414
39:59.700 --> 40:00.500
Good.

415
40:37.370 --> 40:38.170
Excuse me.

416
40:38.970 --> 40:40.800
Are you going to stand there all day?

417
40:41.100 --> 40:41.900
Sorry!

418
40:42.130 --> 40:43.330
Your heart's beating so fast.

419
40:43.670 --> 40:44.530
Just like that night.

420
40:45.370 --> 40:47.570
That lipstick looks good on you.

421
40:47.970 --> 40:49.800
Does this still count as teaching me?

422
40:50.130 --> 40:52.370
My boss is just too beautiful.

423
40:53.000 --> 40:57.870
Beautiful? Since when is 'too beautiful' part of the job title, Miss Assistant?

424
40:58.100 --> 40:59.870
Well? What do you think? Does it work?

425
41:00.270 --> 41:03.070
Do you have a date, or is there a special occasion?

426
41:03.370 --> 41:05.770
Ms. Rinrada, is there something urgent?

427
41:06.500 --> 41:11.700
I'm worried this woman has some hidden agenda behind all that advertising money.
